<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emporio (Chios)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emporio is a harbour site on the south coast of Chios in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, excavated by the British School at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> in the 1950s. It revealed a long-lived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> settlement with links to the Minoan and Mycenaean worlds, and an Archaic hilltop town of the seventh and sixth centuries BCE with houses, a megaron hall and a sanctuary of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athena">Athena</a>.</p></div>
